$termsBody = <<<'PCTERMS'
        <p>These Business Account Terms set out the invoice payment conditions that apply where PowerCabs has approved a business customer for payment by invoice. They are referred to in the documentation below as the &ldquo;Invoice Terms&rdquo;.</p>
        <p>Supplier: POWERCABS IRELAND LIMITED, or the other PowerCabs entity expressly identified in the applicable booking agreement (&ldquo;PowerCabs&rdquo;)<br>Customer: The business, company or other undertaking identified in the applicable booking confirmation or invoice (&ldquo;Customer&rdquo;)<br>Jurisdiction: Ireland<br>Standard payment term: Seven (7) calendar days</p>

        <h2 id="ba-1" class="tw-mb-3 tw-mt-10 tw-text-2xl tw-font-bold">1. Scope and Application</h2>
        <p>1.1. These Business Account Terms (&ldquo;Invoice Terms&rdquo;) apply to bookings for pre-booked passenger transport services made by or on behalf of a business customer where PowerCabs has expressly approved payment by invoice.</p>
        <p>1.2. These Invoice Terms supplement the applicable corporate account agreement, booking confirmation and any agreed service-specific terms.</p>
        <p>1.3. These Invoice Terms form part of the contract only where they have been provided to the Customer and expressly accepted, or otherwise validly incorporated into the contract, before or when the relevant booking contract is concluded.</p>
        <p>1.4. A request by the Customer for invoice payment does not, by itself, create a right to credit or oblige PowerCabs to accept invoice payment. PowerCabs may accept or reject such a request before confirming the relevant booking.</p>
        <p>1.5. In these Invoice Terms, references to &ldquo;services&rdquo; mean the transport services or booking services supplied under the relevant contract. The party legally responsible for supplying the service and the party entitled to invoice the Customer shall be identified in the applicable agreement.</p>

        <h2 id="ba-2" class="tw-mb-3 tw-mt-10 tw-text-2xl tw-font-bold">2. Seven-Day Payment Obligation</h2>
        <p>2.1. Unless otherwise expressly agreed in writing by an authorised representative of PowerCabs, each invoice issued under an approved invoice-payment arrangement must be paid in full within seven (7) calendar days of the invoice date.</p>
        <p>2.2. The applicable payment deadline shall be stated on the invoice. Where the invoice specifies a due date consistent with the agreed seven-day period, the Customer must ensure that the full amount due is received in cleared funds by that date.</p>
        <p>2.3. The seven-day period is an express contractual payment term agreed between the parties. It is not intended to displace any mandatory statutory payment period or other mandatory legal requirement that applies to a particular transaction.</p>
        <p>2.4. The Customer acknowledges that its internal accounts-payable procedures, purchase order processing, approval requirements or delays in receiving funds from another party do not, by themselves, vary the agreed payment deadline.</p>
        <p>2.5. Any extension of the payment deadline must be agreed in writing by an authorised representative of PowerCabs. The absence of a payment reminder does not extend the due date.</p>
        <p>2.6. Unless the parties expressly agree otherwise in writing, invoice payment is not conditional upon the Customer receiving reimbursement from a passenger, employee, client, travel agent or other third party.</p>

        <h2 id="ba-3" class="tw-mb-3 tw-mt-10 tw-text-2xl tw-font-bold">3. Corporate Customer Liability</h2>
        <p>3.1. The legal entity identified as the contracting Customer in the booking confirmation or corporate account agreement is responsible for paying the charges properly due under that contract.</p>
        <p>3.2. Where a booking is made by an employee, travel coordinator, agent or other authorised representative acting on behalf of a business, the business shall be responsible for payment where the booking was entered into on its behalf and the relevant representative acted with actual or legally recognised authority.</p>
        <p>3.3. A person making a booking on behalf of a business must provide accurate company details, billing information and any agreed purchase order or account reference.</p>
        <p>3.4. A Customer may not avoid a contractual payment obligation merely because the passenger differs from the person who made the booking or because the passenger is an employee, director, client, guest or other nominated traveller.</p>
        <p>3.5. Nothing in this clause makes an employee, passenger, director or other individual personally liable for a corporate debt unless that individual separately assumes such liability under a legally valid agreement.</p>
        <p>3.6. Where a booking is made through an intermediary, the identity of the contracting Customer and the party liable for payment shall be determined by the relevant booking agreement and the circumstances in which the contract was made.</p>

        <h2 id="ba-4" class="tw-mb-3 tw-mt-10 tw-text-2xl tw-font-bold">4. Booking Confirmation and Charges</h2>
        <p>4.1. The Customer shall pay the agreed charges for each confirmed booking in accordance with the applicable quotation, corporate rate agreement, booking confirmation or other binding pricing arrangement.</p>
        <p>4.2. Where a journey price is agreed in advance, the booking documentation should identify the journey, the agreed charge and any applicable additional charges, including waiting time, parking, tolls, additional stops or changes requested by the Customer, where those charges have been disclosed and contractually agreed.</p>
        <p>4.3. No additional charge shall be imposed unless it is permitted by the applicable agreement and relevant law.</p>
        <p>4.4. Where applicable taxi or Small Public Service Vehicle (&ldquo;SPSV&rdquo;) rules require a particular fare arrangement or written agreement, PowerCabs and the relevant transport provider shall comply with those requirements. Nothing in these Invoice Terms overrides any mandatory fare-calculation requirement.</p>
        <p>4.5. The Customer must notify PowerCabs promptly of any material discrepancy in an invoice and provide sufficient information to identify the booking and the disputed amount.</p>

        <h2 id="ba-5" class="tw-mb-3 tw-mt-10 tw-text-2xl tw-font-bold">5. Invoices and Payment Method</h2>
        <p>5.1. PowerCabs may issue invoices electronically to the billing address or email address nominated by the Customer, subject to applicable legal requirements.</p>
        <p>5.2. The Customer must pay using a payment method accepted by PowerCabs and specified on the invoice or otherwise agreed in writing.</p>
        <p>5.3. Payment must be made in the currency specified on the invoice, quoting the relevant invoice number or reference.</p>
        <p>5.4. The Customer shall not make an unauthorised deduction or set-off against an invoice, subject to any right of deduction, set-off or withholding that cannot lawfully be excluded.</p>
        <p>5.5. An invoice shall not be treated as paid merely because the Customer has initiated a transfer or supplied a remittance advice. Payment is ordinarily completed when the funds are received in cleared form by the designated recipient, subject to applicable law and any contrary agreement.</p>

        <h2 id="ba-6" class="tw-mb-3 tw-mt-10 tw-text-2xl tw-font-bold">6. Overdue Invoices and Formal Demand</h2>
        <p>6.1. Where an amount properly due remains unpaid after its contractual due date, PowerCabs may record the invoice as overdue and request payment from the Customer.</p>
        <p>6.2. PowerCabs may issue a written payment reminder or formal letter of demand identifying the invoice, outstanding principal, applicable interest and any other amount lawfully recoverable.</p>
        <p>6.3. Failure to pay by the agreed deadline may constitute a breach of contract and entitle PowerCabs to pursue available contractual and statutory remedies.</p>
        <p>6.4. The issue of a reminder, the allowance of additional time to pay or the acceptance of part-payment does not, by itself, waive PowerCabs&rsquo; rights in respect of the remaining debt.</p>
        <p>6.5. Where a genuine dispute is raised, PowerCabs may investigate the matter and request supporting documents. The existence of a dispute shall not automatically extinguish an otherwise valid debt, and any undisputed amount remains payable in accordance with the contract, subject to applicable law.</p>

        <h2 id="ba-7" class="tw-mb-3 tw-mt-10 tw-text-2xl tw-font-bold">7. Statutory Late-Payment Interest</h2>
        <p>7.1. In respect of qualifying commercial transactions governed by the European Communities (Late Payment in Commercial Transactions) Regulations 2012, as amended, PowerCabs reserves all rights to statutory late-payment interest.</p>
        <p>7.2. Where applicable, statutory late-payment interest shall accrue on the overdue amount from the day following the relevant contractual payment date until payment, in accordance with the applicable legislation.</p>
        <p>7.3. Unless a different lawful contractual rate applies, the statutory rate is based on the relevant European Central Bank reference rate plus eight percentage points, as prescribed by the legislation.</p>
        <p>7.4. The right to statutory late-payment interest arises subject to the statutory conditions, including the supplier having fulfilled its relevant contractual and legal obligations and the late payment being attributable to the purchaser as required by law.</p>
        <p>7.5. No provision of these Invoice Terms shall be interpreted as excluding or waiving a statutory entitlement to late-payment interest that cannot lawfully be excluded or waived.</p>

        <h2 id="ba-8" class="tw-mb-3 tw-mt-10 tw-text-2xl tw-font-bold">8. Statutory Compensation for Recovery Costs</h2>
        <p>8.1. Where statutory late-payment interest becomes payable in a qualifying commercial transaction, PowerCabs reserves its right to the fixed compensation for recovery costs provided under Regulation 9 and the Schedule to the European Communities (Late Payment in Commercial Transactions) Regulations 2012, as amended.</p>
        <p>8.2. The applicable statutory compensation is determined by the amount of the relevant overdue invoice:</p>
        <ul class="tw-mb-4 tw-ml-5 tw-flex tw-list-none tw-flex-col tw-gap-1.5 tw-p-0">
          <li>(a) &euro;40 where the amount due does not exceed &euro;1,000;</li>
          <li>(b) &euro;70 where the amount due exceeds &euro;1,000 but does not exceed &euro;10,000; or</li>
          <li>(c) &euro;100 where the amount due exceeds &euro;10,000.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>8.3. Where permitted by the applicable legislation, PowerCabs may also seek reasonable compensation for relevant recovery costs exceeding the applicable fixed statutory compensation, including reasonable costs incurred in instructing a solicitor or debt-recovery agency.</p>
        <p>8.4. Any additional recovery costs claimed must be legally recoverable and, where required, reasonable and properly attributable to recovery of the overdue debt. This clause does not impose an arbitrary penalty or guarantee recovery of every cost incurred.</p>
        <p>8.5. The statutory interest and recovery-cost provisions apply only to the extent that the relevant legislation applies to the transaction and the relevant statutory conditions are satisfied.</p>

        <h2 id="ba-9" class="tw-mb-3 tw-mt-10 tw-text-2xl tw-font-bold">9. Disputed Invoices and Undisputed Amounts</h2>
        <p>9.1. The Customer must notify PowerCabs in writing promptly if it disputes an invoice, identifying the relevant invoice, the amount disputed and the grounds of the dispute.</p>
        <p>9.2. The parties shall cooperate in good faith to investigate and resolve a properly notified dispute.</p>
        <p>9.3. Unless otherwise agreed in writing or required by law, the Customer shall pay any amount that is not genuinely disputed by the applicable due date.</p>
        <p>9.4. Neither party is required by this clause to waive a valid contractual defence or statutory right. A notification of dispute shall not automatically suspend payment of all sums where only part of an invoice is disputed.</p>

        <h2 id="ba-10" class="tw-mb-3 tw-mt-10 tw-text-2xl tw-font-bold">10. Suspension of Invoice Privileges and Future Bookings</h2>
        <p>10.1. Where the Customer has overdue invoices, PowerCabs may review, suspend or withdraw the Customer&rsquo;s eligibility for future invoice payment, subject to the relevant agreement and applicable law.</p>
        <p>10.2. PowerCabs may require advance payment or another approved payment method for future bookings where permitted by the relevant agreement.</p>
        <p>10.3. The suspension or withdrawal of invoice privileges does not, by itself, cancel an existing confirmed booking or extinguish any payment obligation already incurred.</p>
        <p>10.4. Cancellation, suspension or refusal to perform an existing confirmed booking must be consistent with the applicable booking contract, any relevant notice requirements and applicable law.</p>
        <p>10.5. Any cancellation charge or other amount claimed must be supported by the applicable agreement and must not constitute an unlawful penalty.</p>

        <h2 id="ba-11" class="tw-mb-3 tw-mt-10 tw-text-2xl tw-font-bold">11. Recovery of Unpaid Debts and Legal Proceedings</h2>
        <p>11.1. If the Customer fails to pay an amount properly due, PowerCabs may take lawful steps to recover the debt, including sending a formal letter of demand, instructing a solicitor or authorised debt-recovery provider and commencing proceedings before a competent court.</p>
        <p>11.2. Subject to applicable law and the relevant court&rsquo;s powers, PowerCabs may seek recovery of:</p>
        <ul class="tw-mb-4 tw-ml-5 tw-flex tw-list-none tw-flex-col tw-gap-1.5 tw-p-0">
          <li>(a) the outstanding principal debt;</li>
          <li>(b) applicable statutory or other legally recoverable interest;</li>
          <li>(c) statutory compensation for recovery costs, where applicable; and</li>
          <li>(d) such further costs or expenses as are recoverable under the contract, legislation or an order of a competent court.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>11.3. The Customer acknowledges that an unpaid invoice may be relied upon as evidence of the amount claimed, together with the booking confirmation, service records, contractual terms, relevant correspondence and any other admissible evidence.</p>
        <p>11.4. If judgment is obtained, PowerCabs may pursue lawful enforcement procedures available under Irish law.</p>
        <p>11.5. Nothing in this clause guarantees a particular legal outcome or removes the requirement to establish the debt and comply with applicable court procedures.</p>

        <h2 id="ba-12" class="tw-mb-3 tw-mt-10 tw-text-2xl tw-font-bold">12. Passenger Transport and Regulatory Compliance</h2>
        <p>12.1. All transport services shall be provided in accordance with the legislation and regulatory requirements applicable to the relevant service and transport provider.</p>
        <p>12.2. Where the journey is supplied as a taxi service subject to the SPSV regulatory framework, the relevant fare must be calculated in accordance with the applicable rules unless a lawful alternative arrangement applies.</p>
        <p>12.3. Where a pre-agreed taxi fare is relied upon instead of taximeter calculation, the required prior written agreement must identify the agreed charge and contain the required confirmation concerning the passenger&rsquo;s waiver of the right to have the fare calculated using the taximeter, where that waiver is legally applicable.</p>
        <p>12.4. These Invoice Terms govern the payment obligations between PowerCabs and the corporate Customer. They do not override any mandatory rights or protections applying to the passenger or any regulatory obligation imposed on the driver, vehicle owner, transport operator or booking service provider.</p>
        <p>12.5. Where PowerCabs acts as a booking intermediary rather than the direct supplier of a journey, the relevant booking documentation shall accurately identify the transport provider and the respective responsibilities of the parties.</p>

        <h2 id="ba-13" class="tw-mb-3 tw-mt-10 tw-text-2xl tw-font-bold">13. Notices and Records</h2>
        <p>13.1. The Customer shall maintain accurate billing and contact details and promptly notify PowerCabs of any change.</p>
        <p>13.2. Invoices and payment reminders may be sent to the agreed business email address or other agreed communication channel.</p>
        <p>13.3. The parties should retain the booking confirmation, applicable terms, invoice, payment records and relevant correspondence for evidential and accounting purposes, subject to applicable data-protection and record-retention requirements.</p>

        <h2 id="ba-14" class="tw-mb-3 tw-mt-10 tw-text-2xl tw-font-bold">14. Governing Law and Jurisdiction</h2>
        <p>14.1. These Invoice Terms and the relevant contractual payment obligations shall be governed by the laws of Ireland, subject to any mandatory applicable law.</p>
        <p>14.2. Any proceedings to recover an unpaid invoice shall be brought before a court of competent jurisdiction in accordance with applicable Irish law and court rules.</p>
        <p>14.3. Nothing in these Invoice Terms excludes any mandatory right, remedy or protection that cannot lawfully be excluded.</p>

        <h2 id="ba-15" class="tw-mb-3 tw-mt-10 tw-text-2xl tw-font-bold">15. Variation, Severability and Entire Agreement</h2>
        <p>15.1. Any variation to these Invoice Terms must be agreed in writing by authorised representatives of the parties, subject to applicable law.</p>
        <p>15.2. If a provision is held to be unlawful or unenforceable, it shall be limited or severed to the extent necessary, where legally permissible, without invalidating the remaining provisions.</p>
        <p>15.3. These Invoice Terms shall be read together with the applicable corporate account agreement, booking confirmation and any other expressly incorporated contractual terms. In the event of inconsistency, the order of precedence shall be determined by the express agreement between the parties and applicable law.</p>
PCTERMS;
